"prose": [
{
"from": 253,
"to": 260,
"text": "No boot-path touchpoint (no `src/` file, no wrapper start path): the harness smoke is not a gate here. The live legs are the round; every other entry runs on the fake agent. Entry 20 (revision 1) is the deadline control's entry: it builds the workspace with the fake agent, then runs the case under nextest's default profile, which has no kill line, so a removed guard reads as the case failing, never a TIMEOUT; it stands after the round's span (entries 9–19), so the round's pre-flight finds no non-leg entry inside it. Entries 13–16 are the four starts already fired (revision 1): none is re-fired; entry 14's recorded red stands as its disposition names (its `note`). Entries 17–19 are `R3D`'s round steps and its start, fired by `gate.py run --live-legs --entry 19`. No manifest changes, so `cargo deny check` is not listed."
},
{
"from": 262,
"to": 285,
"text": "The one-shot controls (implement fires them with `gate.py control`, never as entries; validation.md check 4 (6)): - `ready-deadline` — entry 20 (revision 1; was entry 6, which the tool's clone could not build for: UNREPRODUCED,   then held by hand over a whole-workspace clone — in place PASS 2.303 s, removed FAIL 20.340 s, no TIMEOUT,   `evidence/control-2.txt`), `--timeout 1200` (the clone's whole-workspace build, then the case); guard: `start`   reads `opts.ready_deadline`; edit in `crates/viola-e2e/src/harness/boot.rs`: `opts.ready_deadline` →   `INSTANCE_DEADLINE` at the wait; case `boot_that_never_gets_ready_times_out_and_stops_its_supervisor`. With the   guard gone the boot waits the 20 s constant and the case's wall assertion (below 10 s) fails about 20 s in, under   nextest's default profile (no kill line); `holds` = the case ran and FAILED with no TIMEOUT line. - `capture-keys` — entry 3, `--timeout 300`; guard: the key-name filter in `capture.rs` (a name outside   `[a-z_]{1,40}` counted in `other_keys`, never listed); edit: the filter's predicate replaced by `true`; case: the   unit case on an off-pattern key name. With the guard gone that name is listed in `keys` and the case's assertion   fails. Read `holds` by the stopped run (`evidence/control-1.txt`). - `capture-source` — entry 3, `--timeout 300`; guard: the closed `source` words (a string outside the two wake words   reads `other`); edit: the `other` arm returns the string as given; case: the unit case on a `user` source. With   the guard gone the case reads `user` and fails. Read `holds` by the stopped run (`evidence/control-1.txt`). - `wake-capture` — entry 4, `--timeout 600`; guard: the capture sign in `wake.rs` (a capture line past send 1's   mark tells the fired wake); edit: that branch's condition replaced by `false`; case: the `r3` rehearsal with a   capture line. With the guard gone the start stands to its 3 s bound, reads `wake: unfired`, and the case's   `wake-sign: capture` assertion fails; `holds` = the case FAILED with no TIMEOUT line (the rehearsal's own waits   sit under its 18 s WITHIN, far under the binary's kill). Read `holds` by the stopped run (`evidence/control-3.txt`). - `user-config-mark` — entry 3, `--timeout 300` (revision 1, inputs#I6 item 3); guard: the mark search in   `isolate.rs` (a needle found in the moved file reads `changed-by-rig`); edit: the search's found-predicate replaced   by `false`; case: the unit case «stamp moved, the path mark present». With the guard gone that case reads   `changed-by-others` and fails (predicted, unmeasured until implement fires it); `holds` = the case FAILED."
}
],
